@startuml
' Use COMPONENT keyword for boxes, ACTOR for user

actor "User\n(Patient/Family)" as user #lightblue
component "Mobile App\n(Android/iOS/Web)" as app
component "MQTT Broker\n(HiveMQ Cloud)" as broker
component "Care Device\n(ESP32/Dispenser)" as device
component "Backend Server\n(Optional, Analytics, Log)" as backend

user --> app : Schedules,\ncommands,\nrefill
app --> broker : Publishes:\n- schedule\n- config\n- refill
broker --> device : Delivers topics
device --> broker : Publishes:\n- status\n- config_ack\n- refill_ack
broker --> app : Forwards status,\nacks
backend ..> broker : (optional)\nsubscribe\nto all status

note right of app
  Publishes to:\ncare/device/<device_id>/schedule\ncare/device/<device_id>/config\ncare/device/<device_id>/refill
  Subscribes to:\ncare/device/<device_id>/status
end note

note right of device
  Publishes to:\ncare/device/<device_id>/status\ncare/device/<device_id>/config/ack\ncare/device/<device_id>/refill/ack
  Subscribes to:\ncare/device/<device_id>/schedule\ncare/device/<device_id>/config\ncare/device/<device_id>/refill
end note

note right of backend
  (Optional) subscribes to care/device/+/status for analytics/log
end note

@enduml
